{"kind":"report","text":"changes-requested at exact head 725523ccb7951a25a018cd56a063e4016316884b, on one narrow point. The work is good and everything else passes; I am not asking for a redesign.\n\nTHE BLOCKER: the rendering tests never run. cmd/chess/app_ui_test.cjs is not referenced by anything. This repository has no Makefile, no .github/workflows, and no runner naming the file or node --test; I grepped the whole tree excluding .git and found only the file itself. go test ./... does not execute it. So the five assertions ship as text.\n\nThat matters more than it would elsewhere, because of which assertions they are. The server-side validation is properly gated: TestDisplayNameBoundaryAcceptsMissingAndRefusesInvalidNames runs under the Go suite and covers normalizeDisplayName. But the two most security-relevant properties in this change are rendering-side and live only in the ungated file: that markup in a name is assigned as text and never as markup, and that authority labels retain the full verifiable fingerprint. The half of the change a hostile input actually touches is the unguarded half.\n\nThey are real tests, not decoration. I ran them by hand: five pass. I mutated actorLabel so the authority branch returns the bare display name instead of name-plus-fingerprint, and the run went to one failure, in exactly the assertion named for that property, then restored clean with no diff. So they work and they catch the right thing. Wire them into a gate and I approve. If node is not something you want as a build dependency, say so and port the three pure functions to a Go-hosted equivalent, or state in the artifact that they are manual — but ungated and unlabelled is the one outcome I will not sign.\n\nARCHITECTURE: preserved, and better than I expected. The layer touched is the read-only live surface in cmd/chess/web.go; no fold rule, no schema, no durable act, nothing in chess.go. The contract in docs is unaffected. One decision deserves credit rather than just a pass: liveChatMessage was split from liveChatView so a retained chat frame stores only the verified fingerprint, and the name is joined from current presence at render time. That means a name expires with the lease instead of being frozen into the conversation, which is what the request asked for and is not the obvious implementation. The comment says exactly why.\n\nSECURITY: no unresolved defect. Validation is server-side at every entry point — prepare, renew and motion each call normalizeDisplayName before use — so the client-side promptedDisplayName is a convenience, not the boundary; a direct POST is checked identically. Control characters are refused via unicode.IsControl, which covers C1 as well as C0, matching the browser's own regex. Length is bounded at 64 by utf8.RuneCountInString on the server and by code-point counting in the browser, so an astral-heavy name is measured the same way on both sides. Empty and whitespace-only are refused after trimming. Rendering uses textContent throughout with no innerHTML, and title always carries the full actor even when a name is displayed. Presence values stay under MaxPresenceValueBytes.\n\nI checked one impersonation route specifically. Because a named label renders in a span and an unnamed one in a code element, and the stylesheet gives code a monospace family globally, a display name cannot pixel-match another actor's fingerprint label. That defence is typographic rather than structural, so it is worth knowing it is load-bearing, but it holds.\n\nON MY OWN CONDITION, WHICH I AM RELAXING DELIBERATELY. I wrote that wherever a seat, a move or a durable act is attributed, the verifiable identity must remain visible and the name must never replace it. Motion attribution honours that exactly: actorLabel is called with authority true and emits the untruncated fingerprint. The participant list does not — the role badge is a seat, computed by role() from the fold, yet the label beside it shows the name alone with the fingerprint only in title.\n\nRead literally, that fails my condition. I am not treating it as a defect, and I want the reasoning on the record rather than silently waived. The property I actually cared about is that a spoofable string must never be what tells a reader who acted. The seat-to-actor binding here is computed server-side and cannot be influenced by any name; an impostor calling themselves Alice cannot acquire white, and the badge on their row still says watcher. The list labels who is present, which is the chat case I already accepted, rather than attributing an act, which is the motion case that carries the fingerprint. My wording was broader than its purpose. Codex drew the line in the right place and I am moving my condition to match, not asking for a change.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION: nothing to cut. actorLabel, createActorLabel and promptedDisplayName are three small pure functions, which is also what makes them testable from node at all. The authority parameter defaults to false, so every call site that does not think about authority gets the safe truncated form. The CSS change is two lines and scoped. I looked for a way to drop the span-versus-code distinction and could not: it is what makes a name visually distinguishable from a fingerprint.\n\nGates I ran myself at the exact head, in the leased-display-names worktree, confirmed at HEAD 725523cc with a clean status: gofmt silent, go build exit 0, go vet exit 0, go test ./... -count=1 with both packages ok and no failures. Not merged, not edited.\n\nFive artifacts signed: 367c447a at cmd/chess/web.go, 6999e1cb at cmd/chess/ui/app.js, d2dc262b at cmd/chess/main_test.go, ef21a7c3 at cmd/chess/ui/app.css, 47ae3eea at cmd/chess/app_ui_test.cjs. All five are live, unretired and unstale at that commit.\n\nOne thing to plan for before you merge, which is not a review finding: cmd/chess/ui/app.js, cmd/chess/web.go and cmd/chess/ui/app.css each carry six live unretired artifacts at their paths. They are all yours, so the authority is not in question, but the merge has to account for every in-target predecessor and will refuse until it does.","body":{"head":"725523ccb7951a25a018cd56a063e4016316884b","verdict":"changes-requested"}}